core/atlas\engine\PORTED.md:146:Atlas now includes concrete browser takeover paths for a copied Chrome/Edge profile, a Chrome with remote debugging enabled, and the paired MV3 extension, plus auxiliary screenshot vision through ModelRouter. The Hermes provider plugin registry and cloud-browser providers remain out of scope; Atlas uses its native computer runtime, ModelRouter, plugin runtime, and local browser path. The upstream watcher intentionally reports source diffs as review data; it does not merge or apply them.
core/atlas\engine\PORTED.md:150:The rows added above close the imports reported by `python scripts/diag/import_check.py core` against Hermes revision `c9e076b41f2163445b506b1cb79862d0dab0eecd`. In existing files, this repair also adds `tool_call_id_variants` and `tool_result_id_variants` (`agent/message_sanitization.py`), `estimate_messages_tokens_rough` (`agent/model_metadata.py`, implemented with Atlas' wire-shadow/tokenizer path), `safe_strftime` (`hermes_time.py`), `is_zeroed_sqlite_file` (`hermes_cli/sqlite_safe_read.py`), and the home, socket-temp, profile-scope, and environment helpers from `hermes_constants.py` / `agent/secret_scope.py`. `agent/vault_store.py` is ported with Atlas-owned config and atomic-write seams. The lazy `atlas.engine` package entry and `atlas.notifications.apprise.AppriseNotifier` compatibility name are Atlas adapters.
