## Reusable knowledge

- `core/atlas/engine_core/PORTED.md` is the runtime migration/source-map authority. Upstream behavior changed to manifest-driven read-only diffs, not automatic Hermes-fork merge. `python scripts/diag/import_check.py core` returned `TOTAL 0` for the touched import check, but `core/atlas/engine/hermes_runtime.py` still had dynamic `run_agent.AIAgent`, `agent.*`, `tools.*`, and `hermes_cli.*` paths; do not claim independence without runtime import closure and fork-absent dialogue. [Task 1]
- WebSocket chat uses `ws://127.0.0.1:<port>/ws/chat`: send `run.start` with `run_id`, `conversation_id`, `content`, and optional tool/attachment fields; observe `tool.started`, `tool.completed`, `message.completed`, `session.title`, and terminal run events. The old-session fault was missing `tool_call_id_variants`/`tool_result_id_variants` in `_rows_to_conversation -> index_tool_call_uids`; after repair, an old-session continuation succeeded. [Task 3]
- Browser acceptance required schemas from `get_browser_tool_schemas()` in `tool_catalog.py` and run-scoped X2 dispatch in `tool_node.py`; the final `browser_navigate` opened `https://example.com/` and returned `Example Domain`. Keep `web_fetch` evidence separate from browser navigation. `hermes_config_sync.py::config_file()` must target `hermes_home()/config.yaml`, not Atlas `config/atlas.toml`. [Task 3]
- `status:"ok"` means chat-ready, not that all components or performance targets passed. Measured first health was about 4.4 seconds and a cold data initialization exceeded 30 seconds; the ≤1.5-second goal was not met. Confirm the target service by port plus `Win32_Process.CommandLine` before reading/stopping logs or processes. [Task 2]

